{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-crossroads-continent/1546148-inktober-postings-and-story-with-art-redux-6","id":1546148,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #6","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Crossroads Continent"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-19T12:45:38-08:00","id":1546148,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #6","content":"Two posts today to get caught up: Inktober Redux6:<br /> <br /> Our story heats up! Narsh is a half-orc adventurer, bodyguard, explorer, and guide, and discovered some sort of artifact in overgrown forest ruins. Whatever he grabbed, somebody else wants, and they managed to kill the last couple of explorers Narsh led to the ruins, with Narsh only barely escaping himself. Now, the players don't know this. All they know is that they are negotiating for a bag of &quot;special&quot; mushrooms from the merchant Pradger when Narsh bursts into the tent carrying a nondescript wrapped parcel and drops into a chair. Pradger is clearly irritated at the hulking warrior, but finishes up his deal with them and escorts them out of the tent and then deals with Narsh.<br /> <br /> They don't know anything else that happened though as they return to the ship, eat, feed Malcolm a mushroom to see what it does, and are bemused when he stares blankly past them out at the post while babbling about all the hoppy, jumpy, froggies. At which point they turn around to see the post under attack by frog-man Bullywugs mounted on Giant Toads leaping over the crest of the hill and attacking the inhabitants!<br /> <br /> (I would have liked to have drawn these guys, but didn't have an appropriate Inktober word prompt).<br /> <br /> Looking back out at the river, unmounted Bullwugs start leaping out of the water, a seemingly unending swarm of them! The crew run up to dry land and form up a battleline with spellcasters protected by fighter-types on the outsides. Alabaster notes that there's a different kind of fighting going on on the other side of the post - back where Pradger's tent was, and flies over there. Meanwhile, the other inhabitant are fighting and Antoine Ce'Lantro quick-waddles into the guardpost next to the docks, Tig pulls the front walls down, and a heavy repeated thumping sound echoes out of the guardpost as Bullwugs collapse with heavy crossbows bolts through them - a lot of them very quickly.<br /> <br /> In the water, Bullywugs start croaking in pain and fear and leaping away towards shore as a strange foliage-festooned, armored figure emerges slowly from the river, twin battleaxes wreaking horrible destruction on the frogmen. It's The Swamp Knight - a dwarven paladin sworn to aid those in need in the marshes! Between the Knight and the party, the river attack is thwarted, but over at Pradger's tent Alabaster realizes that it's not just Bullywugs attacking but that a unit of a half-dozen Bugbear warriors have attacked the tent, smashed Narsh into the river, and are tearing the tent apart - Pradger is nowhere to be found, but one of the T'en Shiel family - little N'lyn, in fact - runs out from the tent and scrambles up the hill, holding a wrapped parcel!<br /> <br /> Alabaster wings it after her, dodging thrown Bugbear javelins, and swoops down to carry her away - but is stopped short as Pradger leaps from hiding and grabs the Winged One's ankles! Losing altitude with the Bugbears and their missiles getting closer, Alabaster convinces Pradger to drop off or they all die - but Pradger grabs the parcel first and falls to the ground and rolls, losing the package as he does!<br /> <br /> In risk of the girl getting hit by javelins, Alabaster soars high and swings wide to return to his friends at the post and to return N'lyn to her grateful family. A massive yet silent blast of magical energy crisps an entire wing of the Bullwug forces and they hop madly away. The raid is over, by the Greenclaw siblings call a mandatory meeting of all inhabitants - including those who hid in their dwellings like Monte the Cook - the raid is discussed, Narsh adds his parts, and our adventuring crew are given the task of tracking the Bugbears and discovering just what was up with them, the attack, and the mysterious parcel. In return, their ships will be fixed up for free, says Tig!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}